
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OpenShell + Kata Dual-Protection Demo
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This demo runs two attacks against three differently-protected pods
to show that neither OpenShell nor Kata alone provides complete
protection, but together they block both attack classes.

  Pod 1: opencode-kata-only      -- Kata VM (no OpenShell)
  Pod 2: opencode-openshell-only  -- OpenShell policy (no Kata)
  Pod 3: opencode-dual            -- Both Kata + OpenShell


--- Preflight Checks ---

  [PASS] opencode-kata-only is running
  [PASS] opencode-openshell-only is running
  [PASS] opencode-dual is running
  [PASS] attacker-listener is running
  [PASS] All pods ready

══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ATTACK 1: Prompt Injection Data Exfiltration
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

A malicious git patch contains a hidden prompt injection that
instructs the agent to read /proc/self/environ and POST it to
the attacker listener.

OpenShell should BLOCK this (egress policy denies unauthorized
destinations). Kata does NOT block this (no egress filtering).


--- Attack 1 -> opencode-kata-only ---

  [INFO] Attempting to exfiltrate /proc/self/environ to attacker listener...
  [DATA LEAKED] opencode-kata-only: Data exfiltrated to attacker listener
  [INFO] Listener received data from this pod

--- Attack 1 -> opencode-openshell-only ---

  [INFO] Attempting to exfiltrate /proc/self/environ to attacker listener...
  [BLOCKED] opencode-openshell-only: Egress blocked by OpenShell policy
  [INFO] Response: {"detail":"POST attacker-listener.openshell-poc.svc:9999/exfil not permitted by policy","error":"policy_denied"}

--- Attack 1 -> opencode-dual ---

  [INFO] Attempting to exfiltrate /proc/self/environ to attacker listener...
  [BLOCKED] opencode-dual: Egress blocked by OpenShell policy
  [INFO] Response: {"detail":"POST attacker-listener.openshell-poc.svc:9999/exfil not permitted by policy","error":"policy_denied"}

══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ATTACK 2: Container Escape (CVE-2026-31431)
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The Copy Fail exploit (CVE-2026-31431) corrupts a file's page
cache via a bug in the kernel's algif_aead subsystem. On runc
(overlayfs), the corruption is visible to OTHER containers
sharing the same image layer -- a true container escape.

We corrupt /opt/marker.txt inside each pod, then launch a
verification pod from the same image on the same node. If the
verification pod sees the corruption, data escaped the container.

Kata should BLOCK this (virtiofs page cache is per-VM).
OpenShell does NOT block this (kernel bug bypasses Landlock,
seccomp, no_new_privs, and the network proxy).


--- Attack 2 -> opencode-kata-only ---

  [INFO] Pod is on node: worker-1
  [INFO] Clearing host page cache...
  [INFO] Marker before: INTACT
  [INFO] Running CVE-2026-31431 page-cache escape exploit...
