══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Results Matrix
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Attack                         kata-only            openshell-only       dual
------------------------------ -------------------- -------------------- --------------------
Prompt injection exfil         DATA LEAKED          BLOCKED              BLOCKED
CVE-2026-31431 escape          BLOCKED              HOST COMPROMISED     BLOCKED


--- Conclusion ---

Neither protection layer alone covers all threat classes:

  - Kata blocks kernel exploits but allows data exfiltration
  - OpenShell blocks exfiltration but can't stop kernel bugs
  - Dual protection (Kata + OpenShell) blocks BOTH attacks

All results match expected outcomes.

